# Origin of the backend API — no path suffix (the app calls /api/v1/... on
# top of this). The browser never calls this directly: every client-side
# request goes to a same-origin /api/v1/... path that src/proxy.ts reverse-
# proxies here (see src/lib/env.server.ts). This also sidesteps CORS
# entirely for the browser-facing calls. Server-only — not exposed to the
# browser, and read fresh on every request, so the same built image can be
# pointed at a different backend per environment without a rebuild.
#
# Prefer a stable, DNS-resolvable address over a host-local one (don't use
# host.docker.internal / a bare IP tied to "wherever the backend happens to
# run today") — this value should keep working unmodified if the backend
# ever moves to a different host, without a redeploy of this app.
#
# Every request from here is server-to-server and never carries an Origin
# header — if that address sits behind an nginx (or similar) gate that does
# `if ($http_origin !~* ...) return 403;`, it must allow a *missing* Origin
# through, or every request from this app gets rejected outright.
BACKEND_API_URL=https://api.chatfolio.example.com

# Apex domain candidate subdomains resolve under, e.g. "chatfolio.chat" so
# that "test.chatfolio.chat" and "chatfolio.chat/test" both reach the same
# page (see src/proxy.ts). Server-only — not exposed to the browser.
# Defaults to "chatfolio.chat" if unset.
ROOT_DOMAIN=chatfolio.chat
